          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 2,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Kannada for to lose heart, then the Kannada for bewilderment."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಮುದ್ದಿಸು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮುದ್ದಿಸು — muddisu — \"to cuddle; to fondle\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅಜ್ಜಿ ಮೊಮ್ಮಗನನ್ನು ಮುದ್ದಿಸಿದರು. ajji mommaganannu muddisidaru. Grandmother cuddled her grandson."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಮುದ್ದಿಸಿದೆ, muddiside."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The noun ಮುದ್ದು is fondness, and a pet word for a little one: ಮುದ್ದು ಮಗು, a darling child."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮುದ್ದಿಸು (muddisu) is native Dravidian: DEDR 4960 lists Kannada muttu and muddu, \"a kiss\", with words for caressing and fondling; -isu makes the verb."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for describing what you lived and felt."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
