        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: ಮುತ್ತಿಡು",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮುತ್ತಿಡು — muttiḍu — \"to kiss\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಅಮ್ಮ ಮಗುವಿನ ಕೆನ್ನೆಗೆ ಮುತ್ತಿಟ್ಟಳು. amma maguvina kennege muttiṭṭaḷu. The mother kissed the baby's cheek."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (I …): ಮುತ್ತಿಟ್ಟೆ, muttiṭṭe."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮುತ್ತು, a kiss + ಇಡು, to put: what is kissed takes -ಗೆ. ಮುತ್ತು is also a pearl."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ಮುತ್ತಿಡು (muttiḍu) is a native Dravidian compound: muttu, \"a kiss\" (DEDR 4960), and iḍu, \"to put, to place\" (DEDR 442). DEDR also records muddiḍu, \"to kiss\"."
            }
          ]
        },
